const L_AUDIO = `LANE: song analysis (music-video structure). RESUME NOTE (2026-10-13 relaunch): fft.mjs, features.mjs, onset.mjs, tempo.mjs, structure.mjs already exist under ${HB}/tools/film/audio/ (earlier run of this lane; import-smoke OK, untested). READ them, KEEP them, fix whatever the tests show is wrong; then write lyrics.mjs, analyze.mjs, ${HB}/tools/film/lib/decode_audio.mjs and the three test files. Do not rewrite working code. Files you own: ${HB}/tools/film/audio/{fft.mjs, features.mjs, onset.mjs, tempo.mjs, structure.mjs, lyrics.mjs, analyze.mjs}, ${HB}/tools/film/lib/decode_audio.mjs; tests ${HB}/tests/film_audio_tempo.test.mjs, ${HB}/tests/film_audio_structure.test.mjs, ${HB}/tests/film_audio_lyrics.test.mjs.
Output: analyzeSong(pcm Float32Array mono, sampleRate, {lyrics?: {text, format:'lrc'|'plain'}}) → SongAnalysis {version:1, durationSec, sampleRate, tempo:{bpm, confidence}, beats:[s], downbeats:[s], bars:[{i,start,end}], sections:[{i,start,end,startBar,endBar,label,role,energy,repeatOf}], energy:{hopSec, values:[0..1]}, lyrics?:{lines:[{t?, text, section?}]}}.
DSP (pure JS, deterministic, Node 20, fast): resample input to 22050 Hz if needed (simple high-quality windowed-sinc or polyphase; or require 22050 from the decoder and document); radix-2 real FFT; STFT n=2048 hop=512 Hann; mel filterbank (40 bands) → log-mel; chroma-12 (A440, octave-folded, normalised); MFCC-13 (DCT-II of log-mel); RMS. Onset envelope = log-mel spectral flux, half-wave rectified, mean over bands, local-mean subtracted, normalised. Tempo: autocorrelation of the onset envelope over lags for 50–220 BPM weighted by a log-normal prior (centre 120 BPM, σ ≈ 0.9 octave) + parabolic peak refinement + double/half disambiguation by comparing harmonic support; beats: Ellis 2007 dynamic programming (tightness ~100) on the onset envelope with the estimated period, then local refinement to onset peaks; downbeats for 4/4: choose the phase (0..3) maximising beat-synchronous accent (onset strength + low-band energy + chroma change at the bar line); bars from downbeats (extrapolate before the first). Structure: bar-synchronous features (mean chroma + MFCC + RMS per bar), cosine SSMs (chroma and MFCC, averaged; optional path enhancement with a short diagonal filter), Foote checkerboard novelty (Gaussian-tapered kernel, half-width 4 bars), adaptive peak picking with min section length 4 bars, boundaries snapped to downbeats; segment similarity = mean of diagonal-stripe similarity between segment blocks (handles equal-length repeats) → agglomerative clustering with a threshold → labels A, B, C… in order of first appearance; repeatOf = index of first occurrence. Roles: chorus = the label with the highest (repeat count × mean energy rank) among labels repeated ≥ 2; verse = another repeated label (usually preceding choruses, lower energy); prechorus = short (≤ 4–8 bars) segments that consistently precede a chorus; intro = first segment if it is not repeated or is low energy; outro = last segment if low energy/not repeated (or fade); bridge = a non-repeated segment in the second half that is not the last; solo/instrumental = repeated-label segment without lyrics when lyrics with timestamps are present; else 'unknown'. Energy curve: RMS per 0.5 s normalised 0..1.
lyrics.mjs: parseLrc(text) → [{t, text}] (supports [mm:ss.xx], [mm:ss:xx], multiple stamps per line, [offset:+/-ms], ignores metadata tags), parsePlainLyrics(text) → stanzas [{lines:[...]}] (blank-line separated, strips [Chorus]/[Verse 2]-style headers but keeps them as hints), alignLyrics(analysis, lyrics) → lines with section index (LRC: by time; plain: map stanzas to vocal sections in order, matching repeated stanza text to repeated labels — identical stanzas ↔ same label).
decode_audio.mjs: decodeAudioFile(path, {ffmpeg='/home/wbterminal/bin/ffmpeg' (env FILM_FFMPEG overrides), sampleRate=22050}) → Promise<{pcm: Float32Array, sampleRate, durationSec}> by spawning ffmpeg -v error -i <path> -ac 1 -ar 22050 -f f32le - (stream stdout into a growing buffer; reject with stderr text on failure). Tests must NOT require ffmpeg or a real song: generate PCM synthetically.
Tests (synthetic audio built inside the tests, deterministic):
- tempo: click tracks with accented downbeats at 90, 120, 128, 150, 174 BPM (60 s, 22050 Hz, short decaying noise/sine clicks) → bpm within ±1.5 (allow exact octave error ONLY for 174 → 87 if documented? prefer correct), beat F-measure ≥ 0.9 at ±70 ms, downbeat phase correct; robustness with added noise and a tempo-stable drum loop (kick/snare/hat synthesis).
- structure: a synthetic 4/4 song at 120 BPM with sections intro(4 bars) A(8) B(8) A(8) B(8) C(8) B(8) outro(4), each section with its own chord progression (sum of sinusoid chord tones with a harmonic envelope), timbre (different harmonic weights / noise color) and energy (B louder) → boundaries within ±1 bar of truth for ≥ 80% of true boundaries, A/B repeats share labels, chorus role on B, bridge role on C, intro/outro roles; analyzeSong of 60–75 s finishes in < 10 s.
- lyrics: LRC parsing edge cases; plain stanza parsing; alignment by time and by stanza order with a repeated chorus stanza.`

const L_JEV = `LANE: JEV client + page broker + planning-task helpers. RESUME NOTE (2026-10-13 relaunch): jev.mjs (1076 lines), jev_broker.mjs, jev_tasks.mjs already exist under ${HB}/tools/film/lib/ (earlier run of this lane; import-smoke OK, UNREVIEWED, untested). REVIEW them line by line against the verified API contract in ${HB}/docs/film-mode-2026-10-13/research_jev.md (read it completely first) and the spec below, FIX every mismatch, then write the two test files. Do not rewrite working code. Files you own: ${HB}/tools/film/lib/{jev.mjs, jev_broker.mjs, jev_tasks.mjs}; tests ${HB}/tests/film_jev_client.test.mjs, ${HB}/tests/film_jev_broker.test.mjs.
Read for patterns (do not edit): ${HB}/rynth/ai/llm_client.js (typed error kinds, one retry, spend counters), ${HB}/rynth/ai/providers.js, ${HB}/rynth_ai_client_test.cjs (in-process mock http server), ${SP}/pilot_design.md (prior-art loop design), and SPEC §2.14 + §3.2 (the pilot sends {state, questions, seq} through window.__filmJev and expects {answers, usage, ms} or {error}).
- jev.mjs: \`createJevClient({apiKey, model='typesafe/jev-1.13', endpoint='https://openrouter.ai/api/alpha/decisions', fetchFn=globalThis.fetch, timeoutMs=4000, maxRetries=2, backoffMs=250, budget:{maxUsdPerHour=2, maxCallsPerMin=600}, sessionId, title='holtburger-film', referer, log, now=()=>Date.now() (injectable clock for tests; this is Node tooling so Date.now is OK here)})\` → {decide({state, questions, sessionId?, trace?, model?}) → Promise<{id, model, answers, usage:{inputTokens, outputTokens, costUsd}, ms}>, stats() → {calls, errors, retries, inputTokens, costUsd, lastMinuteCalls, lastHourCostUsd}, close()}; class JevError extends Error {kind:'auth'|'credits'|'forbidden'|'not-found'|'too-large'|'rate'|'server'|'timeout'|'network'|'bad-request'|'bad-response'|'budget'|'config', status, code, retryable}. Validate questions before sending (\`validateQuestions(questions)\` exported: types, criteria shapes, ≤255 choice options, score 2–10 levels, noul criteria both keys when present, non-empty instructions) and answers after (\`parseAnswers(raw, questions)\` exported: every asked id present with the right type; choice key ∈ criteria; probabilities normalised lookup by name). Headers: Authorization Bearer, Content-Type, X-Title (title), HTTP-Referer (when given). Budget: refuse (JevError kind 'budget', no network) when the rolling-hour cost or rolling-minute call count would exceed caps. Retry on 429/5xx/524/529/network/timeout with exponential backoff + jitter (seeded or deterministic in tests) honouring Retry-After (seconds or HTTP date). Cost: usage.cost if present else input_tokens×0.042e-6. Logging: \`log({event:'jev', id, model, questions:[ids], answers:{id:{choice|noul|score, confidence?, top probs}}, ms, costUsd})\` — never log state or the key. Question builders: \`choiceQ(instructions, criteria)\`, \`noulQ(instructions, criteria?)\`, \`scoreQ(instructions, levels)\`. Key resolution: \`resolveJevKey({env=process.env, home=os.homedir(), fs})\` → {key, source} checking OPENROUTER_API_KEY, OPENROUTER_KEY, then ~/.config/holtburger-film/openrouter.key (must be a regular file with mode & 0o077 === 0, else JevError 'config' explaining chmod 600); never print the key (redactKey helper for diagnostics: first 6 chars + '…').
- jev_broker.mjs: \`createJevBroker({client, page, mode='jev', maxInFlight=4, log})\` → {install() (await page.exposeFunction('__filmJev', handler); idempotent; tolerate 'already registered' errors), stats(), setMode(mode)} where handler(json) parses {state, questions, seq} (validate size: JSON ≤ 48 KB; questions validated), calls client.decide, returns JSON string {answers, usage, ms, seq, id} or {error:{kind, message}, seq} — NEVER throws into the page; enforces maxInFlight (reject extra with kind 'busy'); mode 'off' answers {error:{kind:'disabled'}}. Keep per-seq telemetry ring buffer (last 500) and \`dumpTelemetry(path)\` writing JSONL.
- jev_tasks.mjs (planning-time decisions, spec-like criteria with explicit boundaries, conservative default first): \`pickCandidate(client, {intent, candidates:[{id, words}]})\` → {choice, confidence, probabilities, band} (choice question whose criteria are built from each candidate's words; band = 'act' if confidence ≥ 0.8, 'confirm' if ≥ 0.5, else 'escalate'); \`keepOrRetake(client, takeReport)\` → noul P(keep) with explicit criteria on dropped frames, safety adjustments, min subject visibility, pop-in; \`scoreSiteForLine(client, {line, mood, site:{name, kind, words}})\` → score on a 5-level fit scale; \`sectionTechniqueFamily(client, {role, energyWord, tempoWord, lyric})\` → choice among technique families (static/slow-move, tracking, orbit, drone-reveal, fpv/kinetic, top-down). Each returns raw answer too.
Tests: in-process http.createServer mock on 127.0.0.1:0 — assert exact request URL/method/headers/body keys; parse all three answer types (incl. probabilities in arbitrary key order); errors → kinds (400, 401, 402, 403, 413, 429 with Retry-After then success, 500 then success, 524, 529, malformed JSON, missing answer id → bad-response, timeout via a hanging handler + small timeoutMs); budget refusal without a network call; validateQuestions rejects bad shapes; resolveJevKey precedence + mode check (use a temp dir under os.tmpdir() and clean up); broker with a fake page {exposeFunction(name, fn)} — handler returns JSON for success, error, busy, disabled, oversize; telemetry dump.`

const L_PLAN = `LANE: plan schema, compiler and EDL. Files you own: ${HB}/tools/film/plan/{schema.mjs, compile.mjs, edl.mjs}; tests ${HB}/tests/film_plan_schema.test.mjs, ${HB}/tests/film_plan_compile.test.mjs.
Implement the Plan JSON v1 (SPEC §2.15 text + the JSON example), validatePlan(plan, {registry?}) → {ok, errors:[{path, message}], warnings:[...]}; normalizePlan(plan) (fills defaults: format 1920x1080@30 stepped, transitions 'cut', pilot mode 'jev', capture mode 'stepped'); registry is optional and injected ({getTechnique(id) → def|null, buildShot?}) — when given, unknown technique ids are errors and params are validated against def.params (type/min/max/enum); site references must exist; shot ids unique; durations valid ({sec}>0 | {beats} | {bars} — beats/bars require song analysis at compile time); subject kinds point/entity/player/path with required fields; standingOrder is a single sentence ≤ 300 chars (warn if missing — the JEV pilot reads it every tick); capture.mode realtime required when actor.moves or subject.kind entity with moving:true (warn otherwise).
compilePlan(plan, {song?: SongAnalysis, registry?}) → Timeline {version, fps, width, height, duration, items:[{shotId, siteId, editIn, editOut, takeDuration, handleIn, handleOut, transitionIn, preRollSec, technique, captureMode}], schedule:[{siteId, teleport, anchor, shots:[ids]}], warnings}: durations on the beat grid (beats → song.beats spacing; bars → song.bars; cuts snapped to the nearest beat — or downbeat when the shot starts a section; start.bar honoured; when no song: seconds), editIn/editOut contiguous in plan order (respecting explicit starts; gaps/overlaps → warnings), handles for dissolve/fade transitions (handle = transition length, default 0.5 s, added to the take duration), preRollSec = max(6/fps, 0.25) + per-site settle (not part of edit), takeDuration = edit duration + handles. Shooting schedule: group shots by site; order sites greedily by straight-line distance between site anchors starting from the first site in edit order (stable, deterministic); each site appears once; within a site keep edit order. Also export \`estimateShootTime(timeline, {teleportSec=12, settleSec=5, stepFps=8})\` (rough wall-clock: teleports + settles + stepped rendering at stepFps).
edl.mjs: buildAssembly(timeline, takes:{shotId: {file, fps, frames, durationSec}}) → {segments:[{shotId, file, trimIn, trimOut, transition:{type, durationSec}}], audio:{file, offsetSec} | null, totalSec, ffmpeg:{filterComplex, inputs, map}} — trims each take to (handleIn … handleIn+edit), and builds an ffmpeg filter_complex string: concat for cuts, xfade (fade/dissolve) for dissolves with correct offsets, final fade-out optional; audio track mapping with -ss offset; also \`toCmx3600(timeline, takes, {title})\` EDL text for NLE import. Pure string building — no ffmpeg execution here.
Tests: valid realistic plan (6 shots, 3 sites, a song analysis fixture built in-test with 120 BPM beats/bars/sections) → compile: edit times on beats, bars honoured, schedule groups by site in greedy order, handles only around dissolves, preRoll set; validation catches each error class with a useful path; buildAssembly segment trims and xfade offsets correct (check the filter string for 3 segments with one dissolve); CMX3600 timecodes at 30 fps.`

